pr_comments:
Okay, I fixed all the reported issues regarding the fetching and sizing of the icons. And a couple of unreported ones. Compared to the original submission this PR now includes:

- `TabBar` receiving a similar treatment to `PopupMenu`;
- `Button` having a new theme constant to apply an upper limit to the icon's size;
- `Tree`, `TabBar`, and `PopupMenu` having a similar new theme constant, which is used before the item's/tab's individual limit is applied;
- New methods exposed on `PopupMenu` and `TabBar` to set up the per-item limit from scripts, docs are added and adjusted where relevant;
- Icon lookup logic is improved more, and should now cover correctly all three types of custom classes across the UI.

I still haven't added anything to `MenuBar` (see discussion on that suggestion), neither have I added any sanity checks to GDExtension possible icon conflicts. I can look more into it now, or I can look into it later, in a follow-up (or somebody else can).

Edit: We also can't currently support icons for built-in scripts (for those rare occasions where it might be nice to have). I think it's possible to use the scripting language API to fetch the icon directly from a script. We currently have `get_global_class_name`, which can retrieve an icon, but only for scripts which are stored in discrete files. But the approach for getting the icon can still work, if implemented as a new method. I will look into this in a follow-up, as it involves changing more global APIs.
